    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T1H1SUM10",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: sum stage of stage 1\u0027s partial sum (chain 10 of 10), Y = A1 XOR B1; this extra chain feeds the duplicated carry stage T1H2N5C7.B \u2014 one waveguide per pin. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_f2a2812491004427ae5e08467ee60a92",
        "IdGuid": "e23c21f5-67fe-43d8-8f96-53789cecec20",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
