    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T3H1SUM3",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: sum stage of stage 3\u0027s partial sum (chain 3 of 4), Y = A3 XOR B3; the duplicated chains carry the partial sum onto the operand pins of the second half adder \u2014 one waveguide per pin, so the textbook shared stage is instantiated once per consumer; this chain feeds T3H2N3.B. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_91093a5d1f9a4854972bc5b91f473e9e",
        "IdGuid": "6b17b98d-561e-452a-a633-5a66773c8f3a",
